Z||000000||mckernan||05-09-2001||03:40 PM||||need any information on this project I already have the engine in and everything bolted together I need to wire it all together also I plan on using the 3100 computer hopefully somebody can help||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||05-09-2001||10:06 PM||||I'm surprised no one has answered this post. I wish I could help you but everything I know involves the iron head motors and using the fiero's fuel injection system. If no one responds to this post you can go back into the archives or use the search function to find the information you’re looking for. This subject has been talked to death. Not to many people have actually swapped the 3100 engine in with the donor cars computer and management system.<P>I’m sure someone will help you out on this one. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||05-09-2001||11:34 PM||||I was down in GA today and talked to a buddy of mine that has a shop building hot rods. We had this same convesation today. I was telling him that I planned to put a 3800sc into one of my Fieros and he told me that a 3100 (or 3.1) will bolt right in with no mods. Sounds like a pretty good low budget alternative to me. Find one from a Baretta or something and you can even use the tranny. Just get Rodney's kit to change the shifter linkage.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||05-09-2001||11:43 PM||||I changed the ecm in my Fiero to a style like the aluminum head/ DIS motors use (a 749/730). It was not very hard at all to do. I used the pin out schematic from both ECM's and just pulled out the pin from the Fiero and stuck it into the plug for the new ECM. So far, everything works except the speedometer, but I have that problem figured out. I only had to add one wire- to the knock sensor, everything else was already in the Fiero harness. You can do it!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Lurch||05-10-2001||07:28 AM||||I'm in the process of doing this swap into 88 5spd coupe.  Using 7727 ecm from 90 Lumina (same as 7730 except in underhood can.  Moved battery to front, Ecm mounted in original battery area. I wanted accessibility to ecm without tearing interior apart.  Found prom chip from 91 berretta 3.1 5spd 7730 ecm at junkyard.  Grafted fiero harness into lumina underhood harness. Found incapatibility with 3100 egr (96 grand prix) and earlier harness and ecm. Found earlier 3100 ( 93 or 94) with digital egr that can be driven by 7727. I had to swap manifold plenum with earlier egr to later engine.  My biggest problem so far has been weaving the harnesses together, and finding compatible parts(egr, engine harness, underhood harness, ecm/prom). I didn't want to mess with the newer ecm because of the theft control/OBDII etc. Used flywheel from 89/90 lumina 5spd and 4cyl clutch pressure plate. You'll have to fab an exhaust system and change fuel pump if you are going into 4cyl car.  I'm not done with this deal yet but getting close. These are the things I've found so far, but there may be more.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||05-10-2001||11:31 AM||||For the 3100 and 5 spd, get a memcal from a 90-91 Camaro manual trans. BAWX is the broadcast code I believe and the latest revision. Uses the 7730 or 7727 ECM (same beast, different box). <P>Manual trans<BR>Digitial EGR<BR>HEI<BR>MAP (speed density)<P>I used that combo on some 85 X-11's and 2.8L Fiero's. The calibrations are a bit off, but it works. <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
